            <ArticleTitle>[Lumbago radiating to the right leg as a form of onset of multiple myeloma in a 33-year-old patient].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>415-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 33 year old man who consulted because a lumbago; a bone lesion was detected on a lumbosacral radiography, and finally was diagnosed of Multiple Myeloma. The illness, diagnosis and epidemiology are briefly analyzed, rebounding the rarity of its presentation in a young man.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
